bevy-horizon: schedule texture and memory ops as long-latency (NAK_DEBUG=tlat)

For mesa-switch (https://github.com/danfromtico/mesa-switch, by danfromtico and NaGaa95; MIT)
at 953fa75a, after 0001-0026. scripts/build_nvk.sh applies it; this text before the first
"diff --git" line is ignored by git apply.

NAK's scheduler assumed 32 cycles for texture ops and for the memory ops' arm (Ld, St, Atom,
ALd, Ipa and the rest). On the Switch's GM20B, which shares LPDDR4 with the CPU, a texture miss
or a global load takes hundreds. With tlat, both are estimated at 200, so the scheduler places a
sample further from its use and keeps more requests in flight. It changes scheduling priority
only; the scoreboard barriers come from calc_instr_deps.rs. Switch builds turn tlat on with the
other defaults; NAK_DEBUG=-tlat turns it off. Not yet timed with Skate 3 (sk8 findings 61).

The change is StevensND's (https://github.com/StevensND), from his Mesa patch for the reference
Switch port of the ReXGlue recompilation framework, as carried by masseffect-nx's NVK patch
(https://github.com/nebadasSwifty/masseffect-nx, mesa/mesa-switch-masseffect.patch, by
nebadasSwifty; MIT, as its THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md puts its mesa/ changes).

